stateDiagram-v2
    %% Derived Email policy predicates for Operator records; the canonical ceremony axis is
    %% idp-sign-up-otp-challenge or idp-credential-registration-otp-challenge.
    state "No active Email lock" as available
    state "Email lockout active" as locked
    [*] --> available
    available --> available: wrong code below threshold / EmailOtpPolicy#increment_attempts!
    available --> locked: wrong code reaches MAX / lockout deadline recorded
    locked --> locked: comparison, resend, expiry or cancellation / failure count preserved
    locked --> available: lockout and attempt-window predicates become false
    available --> available: issuance records otp_last_sent_at / failure count preserved
    note right of available
        This is a derived channel-policy axis, not a persisted OTP workflow enum.
        Email policy is independent from Telephone policy.
        Failure counts survive issuance, replacement, expiry and cancellation.
        Only successful ceremony proof consumption may reset the channel failure state.
        The six-digit verifier is owned by the bound ceremony transaction; no identifier
        HOTP secret, counter or identifier-owned proof lifecycle exists.
        Candidate owner, Ticket, browser, purpose, generation and expiry are checked by
        the concrete ceremony issuer/verifier/finalizer paths.
    end note
